- **v6 retrain -- FAIL 2026-05-09** -- The 30-epoch retrain on the v6
  dataset (Phase 2.b) ran on Paperspace A5000, completed cleanly
  (`train_runtime=1850s`, `train_loss` 8.50 -> 4.26, `eval_loss` 7.34 ->
  5.06, exit code 0), and saved artifacts to
  `~/Documents/TableAnnotations/models_v6/best/`. **Held-out evaluation
  failed all three pass-criteria.**
  - **Headline**: v6 averages **mAP@0.5 = 0.0337** across the same 5 PDFs
    (precision 0.20, recall 0.03, mean matched IoU 0.11). v4's
    corresponding average was 0.4688 -- v6 is **~14x worse** and is
    worse than v4 on **5 of 5 PDFs**. Per-PDF: `generic3=0.17 |
    K/makayla1/D/Electrical_Takeoff_page7 = 0.0`. Summary at
    `~/Documents/TableAnnotations/baselines/v6_2026-05-09/SUMMARY.md`.
  - **Failure mode**: the model is *silent*, not noisy. It produces
    only **1 prediction at confidence >= 0.5 across the entire 5-PDF
    eval set** (the one match on `generic3.pdf`, IoU 0.56). It produces
    0 false positives, so the standard "curate v6 false-positive crops
    into a hard-negatives folder and retrain" path does not apply --
    there are no false positives to curate.
  - **In-loop torchmetrics also stayed near zero** across all 30 epochs
    (range 0.0002-0.0010). Loss decreased monotonically, so the model
    is learning *something*, but the per-query confidence does not
    cross the 0.5 threshold on real PDFs except in the one generic3
    case. The laptop's 2-epoch dry-run had hit `eval_map_50=0.0199`
    on its 1 unfrozen epoch (batch=1, warmup=5); the Paperspace 30-epoch
    run with batch=2 and the script's default warmup=100 plus monotonic
    LR decay saw the unfreeze (epoch 10) under already-decayed lr
    (~3.25e-6 of peak 5e-6), which may explain the post-unfreeze
    plateau.
  - **Environment**: fresh Paperspace VM venv was missing several deps
    (`transformers`, `torchmetrics`, `albumentations`, `timm`,
    `accelerate`). Installed `MLTableDetection/requirements.txt` plus
    `accelerate`. Initial `pip install transformers` grabbed
    `transformers 5.8.0`, which uses `torch.library.custom_op` schema
    inference incompatible with this venv's `torch 2.4.1+cu121`; pinned
    to `transformers<5` (final: 4.55.4). All deps now resolved.
  - **`compute_metrics` patch required** at `MLTableDetection/train_table_transformer.py`
    (lines 375-440): under HF transformers 4.55's eval-loop,
    `accelerate.gather_for_metrics` collapses the per-image
    `label["orig_size"]` tensor on its way to `compute_metrics`, so the
    original `h, w = label["orig_size"]` line crashed at the first
    epoch's validation. The patched version sidesteps the
    denormalization entirely by computing IoU/mAP in normalized 0-1
    coordinates -- IoU is scale-invariant, so this is mathematically
    equivalent to pixel-space computation. Verified by checking that
    epoch 1 frozen `eval_map_50` (`0.0004`) matches the laptop dry-run's
    reported `0.0005` to within rounding. The patch is local to the
    training script's `build_compute_metrics` and does not affect
    inference / deployment paths.
  - **Recommended next steps** (NONE auto-started -- pending user
    sign-off):
    1. Sanity-check whether the `models_v6/best/` checkpoint
       (`load_best_model_at_end` with `metric_for_best_model="map_50"`,
       which selected an essentially-arbitrary epoch out of the
       0.0002-0.0010 noise band) underperforms the *final* checkpoint
       (`checkpoint-3810/`). If the final checkpoint is meaningfully
       better, the training-side fix is just to disable
       `load_best_model_at_end` until `compute_metrics` produces a
       useful signal again.
    2. Re-evaluate at `--conf 0.1` (or 0.05) instead of 0.5 to see
       whether the model is producing reasonable boxes at lower
       confidence. If yes, the fix is calibration / temperature
       scaling, not retraining.
    3. If both #1 and #2 still underperform v4, escalate to **Phase 3
       (RF-DETR)** per the plan -- the data-side has been pushed as
       far as Phase 1 + 2 allow, and the architecture itself may be
       the limit on this dataset size.
    4. Curating v6 false-positive crops is **not** a useful next step
       here -- v6 has 0 false positives on the eval set.

